      "id": "emergent_ai_safety_diaspora",
      "description": "A wave of defections from leading AI laboratories occurs as researchers and engineers, alarmed by the total collapse of safety oversight, form independent collectives to develop open, verifiable control frameworks. These groups begin publishing low-level interpretability tools and containment protocols outside institutional channels, creating a decentralized safety ecosystem. The movement gains traction among mid-tier developers and public-sector labs seeking alternatives to uncontrolled frontier models.",
